:INFO
Art. 41a Disclosure of data by research funding institutions
1 To facilitate verification and implementation, research funding institutions may provide employer institutions with data concerning research proposals and funding decisions from a call procedure.
2 Employer institutions shall only have access to data concerning research projects that researchers will be assigned to at the said institution. The data shall be used for the following purposes:
a. preparing statements and confirmations required by the research funding institution in order to process research proposals and pay funding contributions;
b. managing funding contributions;
c. evaluating the use of third-party funds.
3 No sensitive personal data within the meaning of Article 5 letter c of the Data Protection Act of 25 September 2020 shall be accessible through the call procedure.
|

:NOTE
Art. 41a — Inserted by No I of the O of 12 Dec. 2025, in force since 1 Feb. 2026 (AS 2025 861).
Para. 3 — SR 235.1
Para. 3 — Amended by Annex 2 No II 50 of the Data Protection Ordinance of 31 Aug. 2022, in force since 1 Sept. 2023 (AS 2022 568).
|

:INFO
Art. 41b Disclosure of data by Innosuisse
1 Innosuisse may, for information purposes, publish data on measures and projects approved since 1 January 2018 in accordance with Articles 19–22a RIPA on any medium and communicate such data to interested parties, provided that the data relate to the following categories:
a. information about the measure or project, in particular regarding: type of funding scheme, title and reference number, status, start and end dates, issue of conformation, total costs, subject area, sector and brief description;
b. information about the persons involved, in particular regarding: participants, contact person, brief description, company size, stage of development, funding plan, and the canton or country in which the partners involved are based.
2 In response to a substantiated written request, Innosuisse may for the purpose of coordination or to prevent misuse, transmit the data specified in paragraph 1 concerning applications for measures and projects that have been submitted, approved or rejected since 1 January 2018 in accordance with Articles 19–22a RIPA to the following authorities:
a. the federal offices represented on the Interdepartmental Coordination Committee referred to in Article 42 of the RIPA;
b. cantonal authorities or public institutions responsible for promoting research and innovation.
|

:NOTE
Art. 41b — Inserted by No I of the O of 12 Dec. 2025, in force since 1 Feb. 2026 (AS 2025 861).

